Z||000000||Homicidal||08-31-2000||08:07 PM||||Read subject!  I replaced the bulbs, no help.  Only half the filament lights.  What can cause this and how do I fix it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||08-31-2000||09:17 PM||||Check your grounds.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||08-31-2000||09:41 PM||||How do I do that?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mdjoneses||08-31-2000||10:21 PM||||I'm not trying to be a wise guy--but--you do know that only one filimat lights up when you are just using the tailights. If you press on the brake the other filimat should light up. From the outside of the car towards the inside--should be 2 dual filimat bulbs then 1 single filimat then 1 reverse light per each tailight. Hey wait thats the way it is on my 86se. Are you talking about a GT? They also sell lens polish in case the lenses are just lightly scratced or dull. Blah blah blah--Mark86se2.8||||reg||2
Z||000004||Homicidal||08-31-2000||10:35 PM||||Let me put it this way:<P>When I was replacing my tailight assembly (I got a brand new polished one) I also replaced the bulbs.<P>When I turned the lights on, I noticed one side had all the bulbs fully lighted and the other side had extremely dull bulbs.  <P>The other reason I could tell is one side is brighter than the other.  If they were both the same, why in the world would I care enough to post a message?||||reg||1
Z||000005||mdjoneses||08-31-2000||10:41 PM||||My old tail light bulbs had a slight haze on the outside. I dont know what it was from but it came off with a paper towel. Hope this helps.  Mark86se2.8||||reg||2
Z||000006||hugh||08-31-2000||10:43 PM||||You can buy a test light at any parts supply store.Get a cheap one.Turn on your lights and with the clip on the end of the wire lead of your test light fastened to a good ground near the light you want to check.Use the point of the test light to puncture one of the wires,the test bulb should light brightly on the wire suppling the bulb.If you have a bad ground when you stick the light probe into the ground wire your tailight will get brighter and your test light will be dim.This is because your test light will be an additional ground.Follow this wire to where it is connected to ground and clean the connection.I just reread your question.Tailight/brakelight bulbs have 2 filaments.Do you mean that only one is lighting?      ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-01-2000||12:38 PM||||Yeah, sounds like a ground wire crudded up. I think the ground is the same color on all sockets. If that's the case you need to folow that color wire down the harness and see where it bolts to the body. Can't say for sure in Fiero but usually its not far from the lights.||||reg||1
